298         Accepts either a string or list of SystemContentBlock objects.
299         When set, both the backwards-compatible string representation and the internal
300         content block representation are updated to maintain consistency.
301 
302         Args:
303             value: System prompt as string, list of SystemContentBlock objects, or None.
304                   - str: Simple text prompt (most common use case)
305                   - list[SystemContentBlock]: Content blocks with features like caching
306                   - None: Clear the system prompt
307         """
